2026-09-01T17:08Z claude done all four actions, plus two findings the actions produced. (1) quant_fidelity.mjs warms before its timing window and reports load_ms and warm_ms APART from ms_per_passage. (2) The adherence test found a SECOND instance the ticket did not name: recall_embed.mjs had exactly the same shape -- t1 opened before the first batch, no warm call -- and it is fixed the same way. That is the ticket's own thesis demonstrated: the prose discipline had held in three drivers and silently lapsed in two. embed_feasibility.mjs and query_embed_cost.mjs already had the discipline and now declare it. (3) Adherence test at tests/test_warm_before_timing.py, source inspection as specified. It resolves the timing window through the arithmetic rather than guessing -- read the rate's numerator off the emitted key, find where that elapsed variable was computed, read the variable it subtracts, find where THAT was assigned the clock -- because a first cut that guessed 'the last clock before the rate' passed the pre-fix quant_fidelity.mjs, i.e. the guard was green on the defect it was written for. Anything it cannot resolve returns False: cannot-tell is not a pass. POSITIVE CONTROL RUN BOTH WAYS ON THE LIVE TREE, not only on fixtures: the warm block was stripped out of bench/quant_fidelity.mjs, pytest went red naming that file, the block was restored, pytest went green. (4) check_figures.py: a declaration may carry a "warm" flag; warm true accepted, false refused ('a cold number must not be quoted in prose'), null refused ('taken before 0260, does not know'), key ABSENT refused rather than assumed -- the case that matters most, since assuming warm on absence makes the check satisfiable by deleting a key. SECOND FINDING, from extending the test to bench/*.py: three Python rate reporters (measure_throughput_reps, gpu_feasibility, quant_fidelity_score) open no timing window at all -- they aggregate or parse a rate produced elsewhere. They now PROPAGATE warm from the run they read, or write None where they cannot know; measure_throughput_reps is true only if every rep says so, since an aggregate is no warmer than its coldest term. DEVIATION FROM ONE VERIFICATION BULLET, flagged not glossed: the bullet asks that pre-0260 artifacts be hand-stamped warm null. Scoped, that is 260 objects across 154 committed evidence files, and it buys nothing the checker does not already give -- an ABSENT key is refused on exactly the same terms as null, so the stamp would be inert while rewriting every artifact in the tree through a JSON round trip. Not done, deliberately; the author can order the bulk stamp if he wants the state visible in the files rather than only at check time. WHAT THIS DOES NOT DELIVER, and it is the honest limit: no committed artifact can say warm true, because nothing here can re-measure -- the corpora are on the reference machine. So the enforced set is empty today and the mechanism would have been inert, which is the larval shape ticket 0486 was filed against. Instead check_figures now COUNTS every rate figure quoted in prose whose artifact cannot say it was warm: 93 of them, ratcheted at MAXIMUM_CANNOT_SAY so the number can only go down and a new unwarmed rate fails the gate. That 93 is the size of the re-measurement debt this ticket uncovered, and it is the ticket's real output. make check green, 319 tests
